+## Context
+
+`priceOrder` in `src/pricing.ts` passes `grossTotal` as the base to `couponDiscount`, while `Coupons.redeemable` in `src/coupons.ts` compares the date with `>= 0` against `validUntil`. Both contradict the README.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:** make code match the README for coupon base and last-day validity.
+**Non-Goals:** shipping VAT, the 50% cap logic, any API change.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- In `priceOrder`, compute the coupon on `grossTotal - volumeTotal` (the sum of `afterVolume`). The cap still uses `grossTotal` as its reference and `volumeTotal` as already-discounted, as the README requires. Money stays in integer cents via `percentOf` in `src/money.ts`.
+- In `redeemable`, change the expiry check to `compareDates(date, coupon.validUntil) > 0`.
+- Minimum-amount check already uses the subtotal after volume (`orders.ts`); unchanged.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- Totals of existing orders with both a volume discount and a percentage coupon change (they were too low); this is the intended correction.
