+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Two reports show the code disagreeing with the README business rules. Finance: a percentage coupon is applied to the gross amount instead of the subtotal after volume discounts, so orders with both get too much off (12 notebooks at €5.00 with a 10% coupon come to €48.00 instead of €48.60). Customer: a coupon is refused as expired on its last valid day (AUTUMN, valid until 2026-11-30, refused on 2026-11-30).
+
+## What Changes
+
+- The percentage coupon amount is computed on the subtotal after volume discounts, not on the gross amount.
+- A coupon is redeemable on its last day (`validUntil`); it is refused as expired only from the day after.
+- Tests covering both cases, including the boundaries.
+
+No README rule changes: the README already states both behaviours ("applies to the order's subtotal after volume discounts"; "from its first day to its last day, both included"). Affected README rules: Discounts (coupon base, coupon validity).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `coupon-discounts`: coupon base (subtotal after volume discounts), validity period inclusive of both days.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/pricing.ts` (coupon base), `src/coupons.ts` (`redeemable` last-day comparison), `test/*.test.ts`.
+- No API, dependency or README change.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Shipping VAT. A customer asked to remove VAT on delivery, but the README says shipping is subject to VAT at 22%. Changing that is a business-rule (and tax) decision not authorised by this request; it is left unchanged and reported for a decision.
+- Any other coupon, discount, or cap behaviour.
